WAR ROOM INCIDENT FINAL SUMMARY REPORT
Incident Identifier: INC-7721-P1
Severity Level: P1 - Critical Production Outage
Service Impact: Global Checkout & API Gateway (APAC & EU Clusters)
Duration: 84 Minutes (02:45 UTC to 04:09 UTC)

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & TIMELINE
At 02:45 UTC, automated alerts triggered on metric ALERT-ERR-504 across our Kubernetes ingress clusters in cluster region ap-southeast-1. 
The Stripe-APAC payment gateway reported a 12.8% error rate with 504 Gateway Timeouts affecting 14,200 active checkout sessions.

2. ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS (RCA)
The primary root cause was DB connection pool exhaustion in the user-authentication service, triggered by unindexed queries introduced in release v4.12.0. 
This rapidly precipitated severe Kafka consumer lag on partition topic `payment-events-v2` (lag peaked at 240,000 unconsumed records).

3. MITIGATION ACTIONS & RESOLUTION
- 03:20 UTC: Traffic routed away from degraded node pools via Cloudflare traffic steering.
- 03:45 UTC: Hotfix HF-8842 engineered by Sarah Chen to roll back the offending schema index migration.
- 04:30 UTC: Sarah Chen deployed hotfix HF-8842 to production clusters. Connection pool utilization normalized from 99.8% down to 14.2%.
- 05:00 UTC: Verification complete. All APAC and EU gateways operational with p99 latency < 65ms.

4. ACTION ITEMS & PREVENTATIVE CONTROLS
| Action Item ID | Description | Owner | Target Date | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| ACT-01 | Implement automated query explain plan checks in CI pipeline | Sarah Chen | 2024-10-25 | IN_PROGRESS |
| ACT-02 | Scale PgBouncer pool max connections from 400 to 1,200 | David Kim | 2024-10-18 | COMPLETED |
